IRIX target restoration: config, multilibs and startfiles

Bring back the mips-sgi-irix[56]* target that upstream GCC removed after
4.8: the config.gcc stanza, the IRIX 6 multilib fragment with big-endian
o32, n32 and n64 (all three from day one, ADR-0003), the o32 default and
MIPS II/III/IV ISA defaults per ABI, and the libgcc irix-crti.o and
irix-crtn.o startfiles.

The IRIX crt fragments differ from the generic MIPS ones because the SGI
linker's -init/-fini handling requires GCC's init and fini prologues in
separate .gcc_init/.gcc_fini sections rather than in .init/.fini.

The pdaxrom fragments hardcode LIMITS_H_TEST = true, forcing an
#include_next of the target's limits.h even when no sysroot exists, which
breaks headerless configure probes. This repository carried two local
patches removing it
(patches/0001-t-iris-conditional-limits-h.patch and
patches/0002-t-iris6-conditional-limits-h.patch); the series folds them
in by omitting the assignment, so GCC's default conditional test applies.

For IRIX 6.5 the stanza selects use_gcc_stdint=provide, where pdaxrom
wrapped a system header. The required 6.5.7m capture has no
/usr/include/stdint.h (only the optional IRIX Development Foundation 1.3
ships one), so a hosted include_next cannot resolve; provide installs
ginclude/stdint-gcc.h directly, as IRIX 5 and 6.0-6.4 already do. The
deviation and its trade-off are recorded in docs/toolchain.md.

Provenance: pdaxrom/irix-gcc tag 1.2 (2aa3421b), gcc-15.2.0-irix.diff;
the n32/64/32 multilib set in t-iris6 is from
gcc-15.2.0-irix65-abi64.diff. The LIMITS_H_TEST omission is original to
this repository. Upstream 16.2 still ships gcc/config/mips/t-irix6 with
n32/n64 only; the series deletes it in favour of the pdaxrom t-iris6, as
the 15.2 baseline did.

Rebase note: config.gcc passes mips/t-slibgcc-irix in tmake_file, which
does not exist in 16.2. GCC's configure silently skips missing tmake
files, exactly as on 15.2, so the reference is carried unchanged.

diff --git a/gcc/config.gcc b/gcc/config.gcc
index 743421768..0c1cf95b6 100644
--- a/gcc/config.gcc
+++ b/gcc/config.gcc
@@ -2682,6 +2682,58 @@ loongarch*-*-elf*)
 	gcc_cv_initfini_array=yes
 	;;
 
+mips-sgi-irix[56]*)
+	tm_file="elfos.h ${tm_file} mips/iris.h"
+	tmake_file="mips/t-iris mips/t-slibgcc-irix"
+	target_cpu_default="MASK_ABICALLS"
+	case ${target} in
+	*-*-irix5*)
+		tm_file="${tm_file} mips/iris5.h"
+		use_gcc_stdint=provide
+		;;
+
+	*-*-irix6*)
+		tm_file="${tm_file} mips/iris6.h"
+		tmake_file="${tmake_file} mips/t-iris6"
+		case ${target} in
+		*-*-irix6*o32 | *-*-irix6*n32)
+			tm_defines="${tm_defines} MIPS_ISA_DEFAULT=2 MIPS_ABI_DEFAULT=ABI_32"
+			use_gcc_stdint=provide
+			;;
+		*-*-irix6.[0-4]*)
+			tm_defines="${tm_defines} MIPS_ISA_DEFAULT=3 MIPS_ABI_DEFAULT=ABI_N32"
+			use_gcc_stdint=provide
+			;;
+		*-*-irix6.5*)
+			tm_defines="${tm_defines} MIPS_ISA_DEFAULT=3 MIPS_ABI_DEFAULT=ABI_N32"
+			# The captured 6.5.7m environment has no system
+			# stdint.h; only the optional IRIX Development
+			# Foundation 1.3 ships one. Provide GCC's
+			# stdint-gcc.h directly, as IRIX 5 and 6.0-6.4 do:
+			# wrap would include_next a header that is not there
+			# and break hosted inclusion. The trade-off is that
+			# GCC's header shadows a system one on IDF 1.3
+			# installations; stdint-gcc.h's __inttypes_INCLUDED
+			# guard (patch 0007) keeps mixed use with the native
+			# inttypes.h compatible.
+			use_gcc_stdint=provide
+			;;
+		esac
+		;;
+	esac
+	if test "x$stabs" = xyes
+	then
+		tm_file="${tm_file} dbx.h"
+	fi
+	if test "x$gnu_ld" = xyes
+	then
+		tm_defines="${tm_defines} IRIX_USING_GNU_LD"
+	fi
+	case ${enable_threads}:${have_pthread_h} in
+	  "":yes | yes:yes ) thread_file=posix ;;
+	esac
+	;;
+
 mips*-*-netbsd*)			# NetBSD/mips, either endian.
 	target_cpu_default="MASK_ABICALLS"
 	tm_file="elfos.h ${tm_file} mips/elf.h ${nbsd_tm_file} mips/netbsd.h"
diff --git a/gcc/config/mips/t-iris b/gcc/config/mips/t-iris
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..d584e1d72
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/t-iris
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+$(T)irix-crti.o: $(srcdir)/config/mips/irix-crti.asm $(GCC_PASSES)
+	$(GCC_FOR_TARGET) $(GCC_CFLAGS) $(MULTILIB_CFLAGS) $(INCLUDES) \
+	-c -o $@ -x assembler-with-cpp $<
+
+$(T)irix-crtn.o: $(srcdir)/config/mips/irix-crtn.asm $(GCC_PASSES)
+	$(GCC_FOR_TARGET) $(GCC_CFLAGS) $(MULTILIB_CFLAGS) $(INCLUDES) \
+	-c -o $@ -x assembler-with-cpp $<
+
+#undef  STARTFILE_SPEC
+#define STARTFILE_SPEC "irix-crti.asm crtbegin.s"
+
+#undef  ENDFILE_SPEC
+#define ENDFILE_SPEC "crtend.s irix-crtn.asm"
